    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0197" n="185" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg185"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">874.00/4–1345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-13T13:00:00+02:00">April 13, 1945—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3776. ReDeptel 2447, March 29, 8 p.m.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d172-f1"/> The
                    Embassy has received a letter dated April 10 from the Foreign Office stating
                    that the British Government for its part agrees with the US Government’s views
                    concerning the situation in Bulgaria and it has instructed its Ambassador at
                    Moscow to inform the Soviet Government accordingly and to urge the latter to
                    agree to the proposals for dealing with the situation made by the US
                        Government.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d172-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d172-f1" n="18" xml:id="d172-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it instructed the Embassy to inform the British Foreign Office of
                    the contents of telegram 735, March 29, 8 p.m., to Moscow, <ref target="#pg179"
                        >p. 179</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d172-f2" n="19" xml:id="d172-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 1238, April 18, 1945, 5 p.m., from Moscow, the Chargé in the Soviet
                    Union (Kennan) reported the British Ambassador’s note of April 12 associating
                    his Government with that of the United States with respect to elections in
                    Bulgaria (874.00/4–1845).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
